WEBVTT

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:12.340
"Kodomo no Omocha"

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.580
Both today and tomorrow, I've got time to kick back.

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:24.790
My family of four and I are going to stay the night.

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:27.630
Put on an Egyptian front and become a sphinx,

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:30.420
and for an American feeling, Texas!

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:33.420
When you're sitting pretty, with enough and to spare,

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.680
and yet you always shilly-shally,

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:39.890
and your bitter face and bitter
feelings both teeter-totter,

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:43.350
it's time to get out of there!

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.690
I am feeling Ultra Relax,

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:49.860
a wonderful, invincible Relax.

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:52.860
A one-step-above kind of Deluxe.

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:55.860
I may be a little jumbled,
but when I'm called on, ba-ba-ba-ba-bang!

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:58.830
I always feel Relax,

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:01.870
a humble, simple, sort of Deluxe.

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:04.790
Bright! Clear! Alert-headed, peep-peep!

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:07.880
Keep your eyes on me, okay!?

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:36.070
I'm Kurata Sana, a 6th grader
and TV personality.

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:38.070
My Aoki award-winning novelist Mama.

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:40.070
My manager, Rei-kun.

00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:41.410
The white bat, Babbit.

00:01:41.410 --> 00:01:42.410
Oh, that was fast.

00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:43.750
Hayama Akito.

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:46.750
The man who I've announced
is my boyfriend, Take-chan!

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:49.080
Wow, Sana-chan's first essay!

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:50.420
This should be interesting.

00:01:50.420 --> 00:02:00.800
"Sana-chan's First Essay On Sale Today"

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:54.760
And so, Sana-chan's first essay, the one
that had everyone's hearts tightly wound...

00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:57.090
...as she barely made her deadline,
is finally on sale!

00:01:57.090 --> 00:01:59.760
She's worked hard, undaunted by
Drea-Pro's efforts to obstruct her.

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:01.600
The book is selling well,

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:03.890
and the book signings
have also been a great success.

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:10.440
Come on, step right up and have a look!
If I may be so bold as to introduce myself,

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:13.440
I am Sana-chan, daughter of Misako!

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:16.070
I'm the daughter! I'm the daughter!

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:18.780
Come on, come on, I'll discount it
for you! You there, Miss!

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:20.780
Go on, take it away, you thief!

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:22.780
This isn't a bargain banana sell-off,
you know.

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:25.450
"Hcnub a sknaht!"

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:26.450
Reverse it, and it becomes...

00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:28.710
"Thanks a bunch!"

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:31.790
"Gnileef dab a tog evi."

00:02:31.790 --> 00:02:33.090
Reverse it, and it becomes...

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:34.420
"I've got a bad feeling."

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:39.510
"Am I Wrong For Running Away?"

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:42.760
Sana-chan, what are we going to do
about our dissection tomorrow?

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:47.430
We've been waiting for you, Sana-chan!
"Child's Toy" ambush report!

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:49.100
Zenjiro-sensei?

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:52.440
Congratulations on your
foist essay going on sale!

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:53.440
Thanks.

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:55.440
Looks like it's going
to sell like crazy, huh?

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:56.780
With any luck.

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:59.780
Wow, it was so interesting, really!

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:01.780
Especially the part
where your heart flutt-uhed

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:02.780
when you foist met Zenjiro-sensei,

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:05.120
who you looked up to
so much, Sana-chan...

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:06.790
I didn't write anything like that.

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:11.120
Is that right? Write about it next time?

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:15.130
You're Sana-chan's classmates, right?
Have you read it, too?

00:03:15.130 --> 00:03:17.460
Um... is this going to be on TV?

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:20.130
That's right! We're going
to show you two beauties!

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:21.470
--Yay! All right!
--Yay! All right!

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:23.470
We've already read it straight through.

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:25.140
It was incredibly interesting, huh?

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:29.810
Ah, are you Hisae-chan? I can tell.
You're in the essay.

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:31.810
Sana-chan stood you up for
your birthday party, right?

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:33.810
Well, forgive her, okay?

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:36.400
I know bettuh than anyone that
Sana-chan gives her awl at woiking.

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:39.070
Oh, but I'm not at all
worried about it now.

00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:43.070
After reading her essay, I know
just how Sana-chan felt at the time.

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:46.740
We get along so well because
we sometimes fight, right?

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:47.740
Hisae-chan!

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:51.410
Oh, to be young! Oh, to be young!

00:03:51.410 --> 00:03:54.080
Oh, and are you Aya-chan?
You're seeing Tsuyoshi-kun, right?

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:58.090
Oh, my! Sana-chan sure does
write the truth. Right?

00:03:58.090 --> 00:04:01.420
Yes. I am the one you just
got through introducing-

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:04.430
We don't need any guys.
You can just pipe down.

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:09.430
Uh... could you tell us a bit
about how you view Sana-chan,

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:10.770
being her best friends?

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:14.770
Well, let's see...
Sana-chan acts weird at school.

00:04:14.770 --> 00:04:16.440
She acts weird at home, too.

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:18.780
She acts weird at the TV studio, too.

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:22.240
But maybe that makes her really cool!

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:27.370
There's something about her that ba-bing
makes her take on anything at anytime.

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:36.540
Uh, now let's hea-uh from Sana-chan
about how she sees her classmates.

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:40.300
Okay, well, like I laid out in my essay,

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:43.220
Hisae-chan is an openhearted,
traditional Tokyo girl,

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:45.340
and Aya-chan is graceful and modest,

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:48.550
but when she gets
fired up about something-

00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:50.770
What is it, Hayama, and why now!?

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:00.570
Mami-chan...

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:02.780
And? And? Are there any
secrets about your classmates

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:04.900
that you didn't get
written into your essay?

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:09.580
Well, sure, there are actually tons of other
really interesting things that have gone on.

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:13.870
T- those will be included
in "I'm the Daughter II"...

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:18.130
Mami-chan...

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:25.420
"There wasn't a single word about
Mami-chan written in the essay."

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:21.960
The truth is, Sana-chan
didn't write a single thing

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:23.920
about Mami-chan in her essay.

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:25.470
The reason why being...

00:05:28.930 --> 00:05:31.720
Oh, Rei-kun has borrowed
a motorcycle from a friend.

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:36.850
Hmm? Was that?

00:05:36.850 --> 00:05:37.850
Swoosh!

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:39.520
Huh? She was crying?

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:41.900
Mm-hmm, that's what it looked like.

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:46.200
What do I do, what do I do?

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:48.660
But if I had written about Mami-chan,

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:52.290
I would have had to write about
what Hayama is trying to get past.

00:05:56.870 --> 00:06:01.880
And I like Hayama now. I don't want him
to go back to being the way he was.

00:06:04.210 --> 00:06:06.670
I'd like Mami-chan to understand that, too.

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:10.550
Rei-kun!

00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:12.890
U-turn! U-turn!

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:16.560
I've got to go talk to her!
Go to Mami-chan's house!

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:18.900
We can't! We just barely have time as it is.

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:23.900
No! I can't go to work like this!
Do a U-turn, or I'll jump off!

00:06:24.230 --> 00:06:27.400
This is dangerous! All right! All right!

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:35.750
Rei-kun, I'm going to work after all!

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:40.880
"Sana-chan sings"

00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:40.880
She will now sing.

00:06:41.170 --> 00:06:46.170
♪ Faltering and fretting,
too-la-loo-la-loo. ♪

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:51.890
♪ Who was it that did this to me? ♪

00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:57.850
♪ It was myself, too-la-loo-la-loo. ♪

00:06:58.890 --> 00:07:05.110
♪ It was myself, too-la-loo-la-loo. ♪

00:07:06.230 --> 00:07:07.530
You seem down.

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:11.990
Yeah, a little. It's like
I've got a hole in my gut,

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:14.870
and the wind is blowing through
at 1 meter per second.

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:19.040
The best thing when you've got
a cold heart is some hot cocoa.

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:26.880
Surprised you?

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:28.920
Yeah... sure...

00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:31.930
They said that our scene today
was being out.

00:07:31.930 --> 00:07:33.180
Huh? Really?

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:38.180
Apparently, the other scenes ran long.
We're unexpectedly off. Lucky!

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:42.190
Anyhow, I've got some work
in a movie tomorrow.

00:07:42.190 --> 00:07:44.400
I'm on the Asuza No. 2 train
at 8 o'clock sharp

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:45.520
for a location shoot in Yatsugatake.

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:49.190
I'll be playing
"snowbound disaster victim C."

00:07:49.190 --> 00:07:51.200
See you at next week's taping.

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:54.240
Bye.

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:06.380
I hope this helps to cheer you up.

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:14.840
"Akasaka Hotel French cuisine
full course Complimentary ticket"

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:16.220
French cuisine?

00:08:16.220 --> 00:08:20.890
I got it yesterday. It's a leftover
from a New Year's party. Want to go?

00:08:20.890 --> 00:08:25.900
Really!? But Take-chan, wouldn't you
rather take one of these to this?

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:30.570
But I will be going
with one of these, Sana-chan.

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:31.570
Uh-huh!

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:34.820
"Sana-chan sure did cheer up
all of a sudden."

00:08:34.820 --> 00:08:36.820
Huh? Mami-chan isn't here?

00:08:36.820 --> 00:08:39.830
Huh? Huh? Sana-chan, by any chance,
have you not yet?

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:40.490
Yeah...

00:08:40.490 --> 00:08:43.830
You're kidding! You still
haven't talked to Mami-chan!?

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:47.500
Have you even called her?

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:49.840
No, I haven't.

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:52.800
It looks like Mami-chan
is fairly bummed out

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:54.510
about not seeing her name in print.

00:08:54.510 --> 00:08:57.510
She was really looking forward
to reading the essay,

00:08:57.510 --> 00:08:59.510
asking when it was coming out, and all.

00:08:59.510 --> 00:09:02.180
Sana-chan, hang in there.
We're behind you!

00:09:02.180 --> 00:09:05.480
Besides, I'm looking forward to
reading your essay, Sana-chan.

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:14.780
Mm-hmm! I'm going, I'm going!

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:16.860
After school is over, I'll do
a hundred Komawari right-spins,

00:09:16.860 --> 00:09:19.660
and zip over there at Shumacher speed!

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:27.330
"What Hayama is concerned about is..."

00:09:24.210 --> 00:09:27.420
Hayama... Hmm, that's a
tough position to be in, huh?

00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:32.510
Mm-hmm, I'm all right.
I just have a touch of a cold.

00:09:32.510 --> 00:09:35.170
You know, Sana-chan is
pretty worried about you.

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:36.970
She said she'd go over
to see you right away.

00:09:36.970 --> 00:09:39.180
She's probably nearly there already.

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:42.520
I'll bet she wants to apologize.

00:09:42.520 --> 00:09:46.520
So just wait there for her, okay?
And be sure to come to school tomorrow.

00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:47.850
Yeah, she's fine.

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:50.190
Aya-chan...

00:09:50.190 --> 00:09:52.400
Tsuyoshi-kun?

00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:54.900
"What did Tsuyoshi-kun bring
to the conversation?"

00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:54.940
Tsuyoshi-kun seems to have
a serious look on his face.

00:09:59.870 --> 00:10:04.870
I'll tell her how I really feel...
as best I can...

00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:09.960
But will that be enough
for Mami-chan to understand me?

00:10:15.210 --> 00:10:18.880
Sana-chan didn't want to write
about what Akito-kun did in the past,

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:21.220
so she couldn't write
about Mami-chan, either.

00:10:21.220 --> 00:10:22.560
So that's why.

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:25.020
Oh, dear. I didn't know about that,

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:27.560
and I've been thinking awful things
about Sana-chan to myself.

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:32.150
Having bullied Mami-chan has also
become a scar on Akito-kun's heart.

00:10:32.150 --> 00:10:36.740
Sana-chan knows that he is
quite distraught over it.

00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:42.070
Just then, Sana-chan was
also quite distraught!

00:10:47.660 --> 00:10:49.960
"What about Mami-chan?"

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:50.000
Sana-chan, what about Mami-chan?

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:52.920
Sana-chan...

00:10:55.170 --> 00:10:57.420
I've been expecting you.

00:10:58.840 --> 00:11:03.510
Take-chan! Very handsome.
That looks good on you.

00:11:03.510 --> 00:11:06.180
You look like a real magician.

00:11:06.180 --> 00:11:08.180
Oh, you think so?

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:11.190
Oh no, sorry, I came dressed
in my normal clothes.

00:11:11.190 --> 00:11:13.190
I had to rush over here, and all.

00:11:13.190 --> 00:11:16.530
That's okay, that's okay. Let's go.

00:11:16.530 --> 00:11:18.190
It's the lounge on the top floor.

00:11:18.190 --> 00:11:22.110
The night view will be pretty, I'm sure-

00:11:23.530 --> 00:11:25.870
Surprised you?

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:27.870
Take-chan, let's give that up.

00:11:27.870 --> 00:11:30.120
Poor taste, 120 points!

00:11:35.840 --> 00:11:42.720
"Babbit's drawing song"

00:11:36.670 --> 00:11:38.670
♪ Rice cake, bump, bump,
line, line, triangle, ♪

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:40.670
♪ raindrop with a heart in it,
draw the wings, ♪

00:11:40.670 --> 00:11:42.720
♪ and it's Babbit! ♪

00:11:43.340 --> 00:11:45.350
What would you like to drink
before your meal?

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:49.680
I'll have the red house wine.
And for the lady here... let's see...

00:11:49.680 --> 00:11:51.020
--Milk!
--Milk!

00:11:51.020 --> 00:11:55.310
M- ilk, you say? Very well.

00:11:59.690 --> 00:12:01.990
It would be a shame
if you spilled your milk.

00:12:03.030 --> 00:12:05.370
Huh?! A bib!?

00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:07.450
What am I, a baby?

00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:14.040
I wonder why it is...

00:12:14.040 --> 00:12:17.710
--Whenever I'm with Take-chan,
I feel relaxed.
--Doing movies is great.

00:12:17.710 --> 00:12:19.260
--It's like my whole body feels all warm.
--Tomorrow's location shoot at Yatsugatake

00:12:19.260 --> 00:12:21.380
--It's like my whole body feels all warm.
--will be my first one in a long time.

00:12:21.380 --> 00:12:22.720
--This is the first time
it's ever happened to me,
--will be my first one in a long time.

00:12:22.720 --> 00:12:24.720
--This is the first time
it's ever happened to me,
--I'm snowbound disaster victim C,

00:12:24.720 --> 00:12:25.550
--This is the first time
it's ever happened to me,
--so I'm sure

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:28.510
--and yet it feels so familiar...
--I'll just be hanging
upside-down from a cliff like this.

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:30.560
--I wish I could stay like this
a little bit longer.
--Take-chan, you dropped your meat.

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:31.390
--I wish I could stay like this
a little bit longer.
--It's dirty now.

00:12:31.390 --> 00:12:33.020
--I wish I could stay like this
a little bit longer.
--Huh? It fell?

00:12:33.020 --> 00:12:35.690
--Just a little bit...
and if I could, forever...
--The meat here is lousy, huh?

00:12:35.690 --> 00:12:36.770
--Just a little bit...
and if I could, forever...
--The food at the gyudon restaurant

00:12:36.770 --> 00:12:38.940
--Just a little bit...
and if I could, forever...
--in Aoyama is better.

00:12:44.030 --> 00:12:49.950
I ran away.

00:12:55.370 --> 00:12:57.380
Here.

00:12:57.380 --> 00:12:59.250
You want to use it, don't you?

00:13:03.050 --> 00:13:05.720
You don't seem like
your typical self, Sana-chan.

00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:09.050
The typical Sana-chan would
dash over to Mami-chan's house,

00:13:09.050 --> 00:13:10.390
bust out an apology, say something like

00:13:10.390 --> 00:13:13.350
"I can't hold on to these
worries overnight, heh heh heh!"

00:13:13.350 --> 00:13:16.480
You're our Sana-samba dancing,
"boo on being slapdash"

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:19.690
fireball little girl, usually.

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:20.690
Even I...

00:13:20.690 --> 00:13:25.360
Even I am only human. There are times
when I'm not good for anything.

00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:30.080
Sometimes, I just don't know what I
should say. It would be weird to apologize!

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:35.040
I did it because I thought it was the right
thing to do! Why? Why did I? I don't know!

00:13:36.330 --> 00:13:38.130
I don't know...

00:13:39.670 --> 00:13:42.670
Yo, Piyoko! Nice not to have
to worry about anything, huh?

00:13:42.670 --> 00:13:45.760
And Kurata Sana-chan's
"I'm the Daughter"

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:48.340
shines at first place on
this week's bestseller's list.

00:13:48.340 --> 00:13:51.850
All right! My daughter at the top
of the rankings is a dream no longer!

00:13:51.850 --> 00:13:53.680
Let's fill that vault with money!

00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:55.020
I'll be back later.

00:13:55.020 --> 00:13:57.350
Yeah, come home soon,
my dutiful daughter!

00:13:57.350 --> 00:14:00.020
Aren't you worried about
how Sana-chan is doing?

00:14:00.020 --> 00:14:01.440
Right now, it's about the money.

00:14:02.690 --> 00:14:08.280
I don't want to go...
I don't want to go to school...

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:12.910
Anyhow, I'm on the Asuza No. 2 train
tomorrow at 8 o'clock sharp,

00:14:12.910 --> 00:14:14.040
for a location shoot in Yatsugatake.

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:16.330
Yatsugatake...

00:14:18.710 --> 00:14:21.340
My, Sana-chan isn't here today?

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:26.050
That's odd. I haven't heard
anything from her today.

00:14:30.050 --> 00:14:32.720
Would you care for a bento?

00:14:32.720 --> 00:14:34.140
Hey.

00:14:34.970 --> 00:14:36.310
Hey.

00:14:36.310 --> 00:14:37.980
Here I am.

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:39.520
So it seems.

00:14:42.310 --> 00:14:44.320
Oh, we're moving.

00:14:44.320 --> 00:14:45.650
So it seems.

00:14:45.650 --> 00:14:48.360
Ah, I'm playing hooky from school.

00:14:48.360 --> 00:14:49.990
I've got a taping of "Child's Toy"
in the afternoon, too,

00:14:49.990 --> 00:14:51.410
but under the circumstances,

00:14:51.410 --> 00:14:55.990
I think I'll just skip everything,
maybe... maybe... maybe...

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:03.670
There's something that's
gotten me a bit down, you see...

00:15:03.670 --> 00:15:06.000
So it seems.

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:09.010
Want to hear about it, Take-chan?

00:15:09.010 --> 00:15:10.340
Of course.

00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:14.100
This is the inside of Sana-chan's idol bag.

00:15:14.100 --> 00:15:16.350
Her lonesome Burutcha
is vibrating all to itself.

00:15:16.350 --> 00:15:18.020
Who is that pushing its button?

00:15:21.690 --> 00:15:23.690
Sana-chan! Sana-chan! Sana-chan!

00:15:23.690 --> 00:15:25.360
Come in, come in!

00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:27.690
It's no use, Captain!
Sana-chan is not answering!

00:15:27.690 --> 00:15:28.990
Who are you calling Captain!?

00:15:28.990 --> 00:15:30.360
--Sagami!
--Yes?

00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:32.700
I just tried running the numbers,
and this is amazing!

00:15:32.700 --> 00:15:34.700
--By combining the royalties
from "My Daughter and I"
--Gwaenchansseumnida, kwenchanayo...

00:15:34.700 --> 00:15:35.370
--and "I'm the Daughter,"
we can build ourselves a gigantic house!
--Gwaenchansseumnida, kwenchanayo...

00:15:35.370 --> 00:15:37.830
--and "I'm the Daughter,"
we can build ourselves a gigantic house!
--gwaenchansseumnida, kwenchanayo...

00:15:39.330 --> 00:15:40.710
She's been blinded by money.

00:15:40.710 --> 00:15:44.380
"Yatsugatake is currently
covered in snow!!"

00:15:41.330 --> 00:15:42.710
Yatsugatake is a mountain range

00:15:42.710 --> 00:15:44.500
in Nagano Prefecture.

00:15:44.500 --> 00:15:45.670
Prepare to defend yourself, Take-chan!

00:15:45.670 --> 00:15:47.090
Miracle ball!

00:15:48.340 --> 00:15:51.010
That was a screwball!

00:15:51.010 --> 00:15:53.010
Whoa, now, you won't beat me!

00:15:53.010 --> 00:15:54.850
Allow me to show you something
I haven't done in some time-

00:15:54.850 --> 00:15:57.850
my Gekidan Komawari snowplow step!

00:16:00.350 --> 00:16:01.980
Oh, whoops!

00:16:03.020 --> 00:16:06.360
Ha ha ha! Not exactly Konishiki,
my little Mainoumi!

00:16:06.360 --> 00:16:08.360
Wah! Take-chan, I'm sorry!

00:16:08.360 --> 00:16:12.030
I really have become
snowbound disaster victim C.

00:16:12.030 --> 00:16:14.450
You are a snowball fight master.

00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:18.040
Would you hold me?

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:22.040
Too late, you already are!
Maybe I'll stay here forever.

00:16:22.040 --> 00:16:25.380
Maybe I'll stay here with you, Take-chan,
for the rest of my life.

00:16:25.380 --> 00:16:28.380
Sure. Let's stay here
for the rest of our lives.

00:16:28.380 --> 00:16:30.050
--Really?
--Really.

00:16:30.050 --> 00:16:32.970
--All right!
--All right!

00:16:32.970 --> 00:16:36.640
Together forever
with Take-chan... forever...

00:16:36.640 --> 00:16:38.640
Um... uh...

00:16:38.640 --> 00:16:41.310
Disaster victim guy! Please stand by!

00:16:41.310 --> 00:16:42.640
Uh-oh, time for work.

00:16:42.640 --> 00:16:43.310
Okay!

00:16:43.310 --> 00:16:44.650
I've got to go be in a disaster.

00:16:44.650 --> 00:16:46.310
Hooray! Hooray!

00:16:46.310 --> 00:16:49.650
It's Gojo Takeshi!
At least remember his name!

00:16:49.650 --> 00:16:51.990
This week's Sana-chan!

00:16:55.660 --> 00:16:58.660
I see... Okay, bye.

00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:00.990
Sana-chan hasn't been home yet?

00:17:00.990 --> 00:17:04.620
Mm-mm. Today's the day
when they tape "Child's Toy,"

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:06.330
but she was absent from that, too.

00:17:06.330 --> 00:17:09.000
What could have happened to Sana-chan?

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:12.010
Nothing like this
has ever happened before.

00:17:12.010 --> 00:17:15.090
"Looks like the location shoot
has finished for the day."

00:17:12.010 --> 00:17:15.130
Ooh, looks like they're done
shooting at Yatsugatake.

00:17:20.350 --> 00:17:23.350
It's starting to come down
really hard again.

00:17:23.350 --> 00:17:24.690
Take-chan, where have you been?

00:17:24.690 --> 00:17:26.690
Just doing a little shopping.

00:17:26.690 --> 00:17:28.020
If we're going to stay here
for the rest of our lives,

00:17:28.020 --> 00:17:29.020
you're going to need some things, right?

00:17:29.020 --> 00:17:32.030
Toothbrush, soap, and towels, right?

00:17:32.030 --> 00:17:35.990
A brush, lotion, Heal-Bans,
Q-tips, nail clippers...

00:17:35.990 --> 00:17:39.950
...socks, panties- it takes quite a
bit of courage to buy these, you know.

00:17:39.950 --> 00:17:42.620
Take-chan...

00:17:42.620 --> 00:17:46.670
I think I should go home.

00:17:46.670 --> 00:17:51.340
I mean, my insides were feeling
all tight and stiff, you know?

00:17:51.340 --> 00:17:55.300
But then it seemed like, suddenly,
all of that melted right away.

00:17:55.300 --> 00:17:59.760
When I thought about spending the rest
of my life with you, Take-chan,

00:17:59.760 --> 00:18:01.350
that's what suddenly happened.

00:18:01.350 --> 00:18:04.640
So, I'm okay now.

00:18:04.640 --> 00:18:08.480
Sorry. You must have felt pretty
embarrassed buying me panties, huh?

00:18:08.480 --> 00:18:11.360
I'm sorry to make you have to do that.

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:13.820
You really are amazing.

00:18:15.030 --> 00:18:17.820
You're going to go back, all on your own.

00:18:17.820 --> 00:18:21.700
You're going to go back,
all under your own strength.

00:18:21.700 --> 00:18:26.660
Back when I ran away before,
I couldn't come back on my own.

00:18:26.960 --> 00:18:29.370
That was all your strength then, too.

00:18:29.370 --> 00:18:32.000
At first, I was running away, too.

00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:36.300
It's okay to run away. There are times
when you have to run away.

00:18:36.300 --> 00:18:41.300
The important thing is whether
you start up once again, isn't it?

00:18:41.640 --> 00:18:46.640
Grown-ups like me
often can't do that, you know.

00:18:47.310 --> 00:18:52.650
It's possible that this is a
special privilege that only children get.

00:18:55.650 --> 00:19:00.320
Huh? Something's rustling inside my ear!
Sana-chan, could you have a look for me?

00:19:00.320 --> 00:19:01.990
Here, right in here.

00:19:01.990 --> 00:19:04.330
Hmm? What's this? This was stuck in there!

00:19:04.330 --> 00:19:07.660
A ticket back to Shinjuku?

00:19:07.660 --> 00:19:10.330
There's something crawling
around in my nose, too!

00:19:10.330 --> 00:19:11.670
Ah! This one is an express ticket!

00:19:11.670 --> 00:19:14.670
I wish you hadn't done that one!

00:19:14.670 --> 00:19:16.250
Take-chan...

00:19:18.670 --> 00:19:20.680
Yes, Kurata speaking.

00:19:20.680 --> 00:19:22.550
This is Gojo.

00:19:23.680 --> 00:19:26.890
Sana-chan has just left to head back there.

00:19:28.020 --> 00:19:33.020
Sana-chan just left on her own,
heading back to Tokyo.

00:19:33.440 --> 00:19:35.270
Ah, then you asked Sana to?

00:19:35.270 --> 00:19:38.820
No, I didn't do anything. Goodbye.

00:19:44.620 --> 00:19:49.500
This man Gojo- he may be
someone that Sana needs.

00:19:50.960 --> 00:19:53.540
Take-chan, thanks.

00:19:54.630 --> 00:19:56.670
I seem to have found some courage.

00:19:59.630 --> 00:20:01.880
A quiet manner of speaking,
a little absentminded,

00:20:01.880 --> 00:20:03.300
with really kind, drooping eyes,

00:20:03.300 --> 00:20:07.470
yet with lousy taste, and loves to
startle people with magic tricks...

00:20:08.310 --> 00:20:12.980
Let's see... "Possessing the kindness
that envelops others, the ideal...

00:20:12.980 --> 00:20:14.650
...father type"!?

00:20:14.650 --> 00:20:16.650
You mean, boyfriend!

00:20:17.980 --> 00:20:20.650
Yo, Piyoko! You're showing up a lot, huh?

00:20:20.650 --> 00:20:21.990
I'll be back later!

00:20:21.990 --> 00:20:24.990
"Picture of the new house"

00:20:21.990 --> 00:20:23.660
Yeah, be back soon.

00:20:23.660 --> 00:20:25.320
She's blinded again.

00:20:25.320 --> 00:20:26.990
Oh, Daughter!

00:20:26.990 --> 00:20:30.000
You forgot your watch!

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:30.660
Thanks.

00:20:30.660 --> 00:20:32.330
Yoo-hoo, Sana-chan!

00:20:32.330 --> 00:20:35.290
Rei-kun! Huh? The car...

00:20:35.290 --> 00:20:37.290
It's back! Want a ride?

00:20:37.290 --> 00:20:39.300
That's great, but not today.

00:20:39.300 --> 00:20:41.050
Oh yeah?

00:20:42.300 --> 00:20:44.970
It's all right, it's all right,
I can talk to her.

00:20:44.970 --> 00:20:50.680
I'm going to talk to Mami-chan, and tell her
exactly what I feel. Mm-hmm, I've got to.

00:20:52.980 --> 00:20:54.940
Mami-chan...

00:20:58.980 --> 00:21:01.990
Mami-chan, um... you know what?

00:21:01.990 --> 00:21:05.320
♪ Ha! Chaka-poko, chaka-poko!
The warped one is Misako-mama! ♪

00:21:05.320 --> 00:21:08.330
♪ My daughter Sana is the honest one!
Chaka-poko, chaka-poko! ♪

00:21:08.330 --> 00:21:10.330
Mama...

00:21:10.330 --> 00:21:10.990
Sana-chan...

00:21:10.990 --> 00:21:13.330
Mami-chan!

00:21:13.330 --> 00:21:17.000
Mami-chan, listen!
Mami-chan, you know what? I, uh...

00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:19.340
Sana-chan, it's okay!

00:21:19.340 --> 00:21:23.340
It's okay. You don't have
to say anything, Sana-chan.

00:21:24.340 --> 00:21:27.680
Thank goodness. Thank goodness
you're all right, Sana-chan!

00:21:27.680 --> 00:21:32.680
I was worried about you! Sana-chan,
when you disappeared, I was worried!

00:21:32.680 --> 00:21:38.400
When I thought that you had disappeared
because of me, Sana-chan, I was so sad...

00:21:39.360 --> 00:21:44.360
I understand... I understand that you
didn't mean to hurt me by doing it.

00:21:48.030 --> 00:21:53.040
But still, it was a bit of a shock,
after all... it was still a shock...

00:21:55.710 --> 00:21:56.710
Mami-chan...

00:21:56.710 --> 00:22:04.710
--I'm sorry.
--I'm sorry.

00:22:04.710 --> 00:22:06.420
I'm sorry.

00:22:08.050 --> 00:22:14.140
Take-chan... Take-chan... It went okay!
Take-chan, everything's all right!

00:22:16.730 --> 00:22:19.770
Ah, that was a suspenseful one, huh?

00:22:20.400 --> 00:22:23.320
"A little while later"

00:22:21.730 --> 00:22:23.400
Hmm? What was that sound?

00:22:23.730 --> 00:22:25.610
Ah! What!?

00:22:28.410 --> 00:22:30.410
Aah! What's going on this morning!?

00:22:30.410 --> 00:22:33.330
Rei-kun! Mama! Maro-chan!

00:22:33.330 --> 00:22:36.660
Is this the end of the world!?

00:22:36.660 --> 00:22:38.960
It's all DAIJO-BU DAIJO-BU

00:22:39.040 --> 00:22:41.750
When you sing this song, your worries will go

00:22:41.920 --> 00:22:43.880
Bye Bye Bye

00:22:44.210 --> 00:22:46.550
Cuz your heart will be carefree,

00:22:46.670 --> 00:22:48.470
and your body will be healthy,

00:22:48.590 --> 00:22:50.340
so resolve when to give up

00:22:50.470 --> 00:22:52.260
Bye Bye Bye Bye

00:22:52.300 --> 00:22:53.640
(Sing-ken-ken ken-ken)

00:22:53.640 --> 00:22:55.310
(Tidak apa-apa,
Nday kambay kambay)

00:22:55.470 --> 00:22:57.930
It's always the same old nonsense,

00:22:58.060 --> 00:23:00.400
U-MAI U-MAI U-MAI U-MAI U-MAI

00:23:00.440 --> 00:23:02.940
(Mm? Could be you're fairly dumb...)

00:23:02.980 --> 00:23:05.610
and then later comes the whimpering,

00:23:05.780 --> 00:23:08.150
KU-RAI KU-RAI KU-RAI KU-RAI KU-RAI

00:23:08.190 --> 00:23:10.910
(Ah... it's fine, it's fine, it's fine)

00:23:10.950 --> 00:23:13.240
It's all crazy over there,

00:23:13.410 --> 00:23:15.160
it's all "waah!" over here,

00:23:15.290 --> 00:23:18.500
and the whole Earth
is spinning the wrong way.

00:23:18.620 --> 00:23:22.330
So at this point now, yeah at this point now,

00:23:22.460 --> 00:23:26.630
you can laugh it away, excuse me, I must be going.

00:23:26.670 --> 00:23:28.550
DAIJO-BU DAIJO-BU

00:23:28.670 --> 00:23:31.380
When you sing this song, your worries will go

00:23:31.510 --> 00:23:33.300
Bye Bye Bye

00:23:33.680 --> 00:23:36.140
Cuz you tried your MECHA-KUCHA best,

00:23:36.260 --> 00:23:38.020
to PECHA-KUCHA out a "Hi,"

00:23:38.140 --> 00:23:39.980
so just keep going unlike this!

00:23:40.100 --> 00:23:41.850
Wai Wai Wai Wai

00:23:42.020 --> 00:23:43.770
DAIJO-BU DAIJO-BU

00:23:43.900 --> 00:23:48.690
Once your lips touch, you can't change your mind.

00:23:49.110 --> 00:23:51.360
Cuz your heart will be carefree,

00:23:51.530 --> 00:23:53.280
and your body will be healthy,

00:23:53.410 --> 00:23:55.240
so resolve when to give up

00:23:55.370 --> 00:23:58.830
Bye Bye Bye Bye

00:23:58.870 --> 00:24:01.040
(Sing-ken-ken ken-ken,
Tidak apa-apa)

00:24:01.080 --> 00:24:03.000
(Gwaenchansseumnida,
kwenchanayo)

00:24:03.120 --> 00:24:04.420
(Mou man tail)

00:24:08.630 --> 00:24:11.300
Hoy! In Sana-chan's next adventures...

00:24:11.300 --> 00:24:13.300
Kaboom! Is this the end of the world!?

00:24:13.300 --> 00:24:16.300
So I thought, when our apartment
is suddenly demolished!

00:24:16.300 --> 00:24:18.640
What do I do!? Once again,
I'm without a home!

00:24:18.640 --> 00:24:21.310
Actually, I'm going to have
a new house before I know it!

00:24:21.310 --> 00:24:23.690
What!? The construction is a week behind?

00:24:23.690 --> 00:24:25.650
Oh my, what will I do?
Sana-chan is homeless!

00:24:25.650 --> 00:24:27.980
Next time on Kodomo no Omocha,
episode 47,

00:24:27.980 --> 00:24:29.990
a tale of a confrontation
between Take-chan and Hayama,

00:24:29.990 --> 00:24:31.990
Under the Same Roof With You

00:24:31.990 --> 00:24:34.320
"Under the Same Roof With You"

00:24:34.320 --> 00:24:37.280
That means a ton of royalties
have come in, huh Sensei?
